## Why This Is Asked

This assesses practical CSS performance and layout stability for dense, dynamic dashboards, focusing on containment, grid behavior, and motion design under continuous data updates.

## Key Concepts

- CSS containment (`contain: layout paint`)
- Grid auto-placement and fixed row heights
- Motion design: transforms vs height changes
- Accessibility: `prefers-reduced-motion`, focus management

## Code Example

```css
.grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(180px, 1fr));
  grid-auto-rows: 72px;
  grid-auto-flow: dense;
  gap: 12px;
  contain: layout paint;
}

.widget {
  contain: layout style paint;
  will-change: transform;
  transition: transform 0.3s ease;
}

.widget.updating {
  transform: scale(0.98);
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .widget {
    transition: none;
  }
}
```

