## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of closures, promise deduping, in-flight concurrency control, and simple caching in a realistic data-loading scenario.

## Key Concepts
- Closure-scoped internal state (inFlight, cache, queue)
- Promise coalescing for same id
- Concurrency limit with a slot-based throttle
- Time-based cache with TTL

## Code Example
```javascript
function createUserLoader() {
  const inFlight = new Map(); // id -> Promise
  const cache = new Map(); // id -> { data, expiry }
  const queue = [];
  const MAX_CONCURRENCY = 3;
  let active = 0;

  const fetchUser = async (id) => {
    const res = await fetch(`/api/user/${id}`);
    if (!res.ok) throw new Error('Network error');
    return res.json();
  };

  const tryStart = () => {
    while (active < MAX_CONCURRENCY && queue.length) {
      const { id, resolve, reject } = queue.shift();
      active++;
      const p = fetchUser(id)
        .then((data) => {
          cache.set(id, { data, expiry: Date.now() + 5 * 60 * 1000 });
          inFlight.delete(id);
          resolve(data);
        })
        .catch((err) => reject(err))
        .finally(() => { active--; tryStart(); });
      inFlight.set(id, p);
    }
  };

  const loadUser = (id) => {
    const cached = cache.get(id);
    if (cached && cached.expiry > Date.now()) return Promise.resolve(cached.data);
    if (inFlight.has(id)) return inFlight.get(id);
    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
      queue.push({ id, resolve, reject });
      tryStart();
    });
  };

  return { loadUser };
}

// Usage
// const loader = createUserLoader();
// loader.loadUser('123').then(console.log);
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests mastery of closures, Promise coordination, and cache invalidation patterns in JavaScript without DOM dependencies.

## Key Concepts
- Closures for maintaining per-URL cache state
- Promise deduplication for concurrent in-flight requests
- Stale-while-revalidate caching strategy
- Race condition prevention and cache lifecycle management

## Code Example
```javascript
function makeFetcher() {
  const cache = new Map();
  return {
    fetchMemo: (url, ttlMs) => {
      const getEntry = () => cache.get(url) || { value: null, ts: 0, inFlight: null };
      const fetchAndUpdate = async () => {
        try {
          const response = await fetch(url);
          const data = await response.json();
          cache.set(url, { value: data, ts: Date.now(), inFlight: null });
          return data;
        } catch (error) {
          const entry = getEntry();
          entry.inFlight = null;
          throw error;
        }
      };

      return {
        get: async () => {
          const entry = getEntry();
          const now = Date.now();
          const isFresh = entry.value && (now - entry.ts) < ttlMs;

          if (isFresh) return entry.value;

          if (entry.inFlight) {
            await entry.inFlight;
            return getEntry().value;
          }

          if (entry.value) {
            entry.inFlight = fetchAndUpdate();
            return entry.value;
          }

          entry.inFlight = fetchAndUpdate();
          return await entry.inFlight;
        },
        invalidate: () => cache.delete(url)
      };
    }
  };
}
```

## Demonstration
```javascript
const fetcher = makeFetcher();

// Set up two URLs with different TTLs
const api1 = fetcher.fetchMemo('https://api.example.com/data1', 5000);
const api2 = fetcher.fetchMemo('https://api.example.com/data2', 10000);

// Concurrent callers will observe stale data immediately while fresh data loads in background
```

